    "result_text": "When you open a client, their page now lists the projects you're doing for them. `bin/e2e` passes.\n\nOne note first: your request said OfficeFloor server, but this app's server is Spring Boot (the package is just named `net.officefloor.hq`). I followed CLAUDE.md and the existing code and wrote Spring controllers.\n\n**Server**\n- `GET /api/clients/{id}` returns a single client, or a 404 if it doesn't exist.\n- `GET /api/clients/{clientId}/projects` returns that client's projects in id order, or a 404 for an unknown client. It's in a new `ClientProjectController`, with a new repository query and service method behind it.\n- **No database migration was needed.** The `project.client_id` foreign key and its index already exist in `V3__create_project.sql`.\n\n**Front end**\n- **Clients list:** each row now has an \"Open\" link (`client-open-<id>`) that goes to the client's page.\n- **Client page** (new route `clients/:id`, `client-detail.ts`): shows the client's name and email, with a back link and an error message if the client can't be loaded.\n- **Client's projects** (`client-projects.ts`): a table (`client-projects-table`) that reuses the existing `project-row-<id>`, `project-name` and `project-open-<id>` test ids. Each project links to its own page. It shows a message when the client has no projects or the list fails to load.\n\nNo existing `data-testid` was renamed or removed.",
